{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "brislane-lending-platform-v3",
    "name": "Brislane Lending Platform API",
    "description": "Phase 3 \u2014 API Quality Engineering & Security.\n\nThis collection has a deliberately broken auth setup (inherited tech debt). Your job is to fix it.\n\n## The problem\nAll requests are currently using a hardcoded expired token. They will all fail with 401.\n\n## Your fix\n1. Add a POST /auth/login request at the top\n2. Add a test script that saves the token: pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', pm.response.json().token)\n3. Update all requests to use: Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}\n\n## Security tests\nFor SEC-1 to SEC-5, manually set the Authorization header as described in each request description.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "https://brislane-lending-platform.vercel.app",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "access_token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Auto-set by POST Login request test script. Empty until you run login."
    },
    {
      "key": "application_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "\u26a0\ufe0f FIX ME \u2014 POST Login (add this request)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"test.candidate@brislane.com\",\n  \"password\": \"TestPass123!\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/login",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "auth",
            "login"
          ]
        },
        "description": "## Your fix for the broken collection\n\nThe original inherited collection had a hardcoded expired bearer token on every request.\nAll requests failed with 401 before any testing could begin.\n\n### Fix applied (already in the Scripts tab above):\n\n```javascript\npm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', pm.response.json().token);\npm.test('Login successful - token saved', function() {\n    pm.response.to.have.status(200);\n    pm.expect(pm.response.json().token).to.be.a('string');\n});\n```\n\n### What this does:\n1. Sends a POST to /auth/login with valid credentials\n2. Saves the returned JWT to the collection variable `{{access_token}}`\n3. All other requests automatically use `Bearer {{access_token}}`\n\n### Run this request FIRST before any other request."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "// \u2705 TECH DEBT FIX \u2014 saves the JWT token so all other requests work",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', pm.response.json().token);",
              "pm.test('Login successful - token saved', function() {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().token).to.be.a('string');",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "\ud83d\udc65 GET Customers",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 200 OK', function() { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
              "pm.test('Response is array', function() { pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array'); });"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/customers",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "customers"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "\ud83d\udccb POST Loan Application",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 201 Created', function() { pm.response.to.have.status(201); });",
              "if (pm.response.code === 201) { pm.collectionVariables.set('application_id', pm.response.json().id); }"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"customer_id\": \"C1000001\",\n  \"loan_amount\": 5000,\n  \"loan_term_months\": 24,\n  \"purpose\": \"home_improvement\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/loans/applications",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "loans",
            "applications"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "\u2705 PUT Loan Submit",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 200 OK', function() { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
              "pm.test('Status is submitted', function() { pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('submitted'); });"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"application_id\": \"{{application_id}}\",\n  \"declaration_accepted\": true\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/loans/submit",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "loans",
            "submit"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "\ud83d\udcb3 GET Payments",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 200 OK', function() { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
              "pm.test('Response is array', function() { pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array'); });"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/payments",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "payments"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "SEC-1: Expired JWT \u2014 expect 401",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Expired token returns 401', function() { pm.response.to.have.status(401); });"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "INSERT_EXPIRED_TOKEN"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/customers",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "customers"
          ]
        },
        "description": "How to test: Take your {{access_token}} value. Go to jwt.io and change the exp claim to a past date. Paste the resulting token in the Authorization header above. Expected result: 401 Unauthorized."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "SEC-2: Tampered JWT \u2014 expect 401",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Tampered token returns 401', function() { pm.response.to.have.status(401); });"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "INSERT_TAMPERED_TOKEN"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/customers",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "customers"
          ]
        },
        "description": "How to test: Take your {{access_token}} value. Change the last 5 characters of the signature (the part after the final dot). Paste the modified token above. Expected result: 401 Unauthorized \u2014 server rejects tampered signature."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "SEC-3: No token \u2014 expect 401",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('No token returns 401', function() { pm.response.to.have.status(401); });"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/customers",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "customers"
          ]
        },
        "description": "No Authorization header. Expected result: 401 Unauthorized. Verifies unauthenticated requests are always rejected."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "SEC-4: Rate Limit \u2014 expect 429",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Rate limit returns 429 or 200 (run 15+ times)', function() { pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 429]); });"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"application_id\": \"rate-limit-test\",\n  \"declaration_accepted\": true\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/loans/submit",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "loans",
            "submit"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Run this 15+ times rapidly using Collection Runner to trigger rate limiting. Expected: 429 Too Many Requests after threshold is exceeded."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "SEC-5: Cross-customer access \u2014 expect 403",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Cross-customer access blocked (401 or 403)', function() { pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([401, 403]); });"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/customers/C1999999/loans",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "customers",
            "C1999999",
            "loans"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Use your own token to try to access a different customer's data. Expected: 403 Forbidden. Verifies role-based access controls."
      }
    }
  ]
